    "details": {
      "description": "<p>An orb of twisting primal thorns and magic appears atop the altar in the center of the Apex.</p>",
      "disable": "<p>The orb can be disabled using @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.cYdz2grcOcRt4jk6]{Disable a Device} with @Check[athletics|dc:34|traits:action:disable-a-device]{Athletics}, @Check[nature|dc:34|traits:action:disable-a-device]{Nature}, @Check[religion|dc:34|traits:action:disable-a-device]{Religion}, or @Check[thievery|dc:34|traits:action:disable-a-device]{Thievery}.</p><p>Three successes are required to completely disable this hazard. Each success reduces the radius of the hazard's Tangled Briar Thicket by 15ft (a Critical Success to Disable counts as two successes, reducing the radius it by 30ft).</p><p>The hazard can also be disabled by a creature casting a prepared or spontaneous spell with the Void trait while adjacent to the orb. The spell rank must be at least APL/2 -1 (round up), and this causes the spell to be consumed entirely by the orb. The spell has none of its usual effects. The caster attempts a Counteract check with the same DC as the Disable DC for the Religion skill, but they get one degree of success higher than they roll.</p>",
      "isComplex": true,
      "level": {
        "value": 14
      },
      "publication": {
        "authors": "Locke",
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true,
        "title": "Covalon - Briarmurk"
      },
      "reset": "<p>The orb is dormant for 24 hours.</p>",
      "routine": "<p>(1 action) The hazard uses Tangled Briar Thicket.</p>"
    },
